cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it."
title: "Automated OpenFOAM VOF Simulation and Surrogate Modelling of Dam-Break Impact Loads on an Obstacle"
authors:
  - family-names: Bainbridge
    given-names: Thomas
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ThomasBainbridge/dambreak-surrogate"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - OpenFOAM
  - volume of fluid
  - dam break
  - surrogate modelling
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
abstract: >
  An automated 403-case OpenFOAM interFoam (VOF) database of dam-break surges
  striking an obstacle, varying the water-column height and the obstacle's
  height and position. Robust impact metrics are extracted from every run.
  Scalar surrogates and a POD field surrogate for the free surface are trained
  on a 343-case grid and validated on 60 off-grid geometries, showing which
  impact loads a surrogate can predict and which it cannot.
